<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bleiburg repatriations</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bleiburg <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/repatriation-of-cultural-property">repatriations</a> took place in May 1945, when British forces in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> refused the surrender of retreating soldiers of the Independent State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> and accompanying civilians near the town of Bleiburg and handed them over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslav-partisans">Yugoslav Partisans</a>. Many tens of thousands were killed in mass executions or died on forced marches. The events remain a sensitive subject in Croatian memory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bleiburg-repatriations.jpg" alt="Bleiburg repatriations" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ratni_zarobljenici_kod_Bleiburga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
